# Rust
/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.bak

# Node / Next.js
node_modules
.next
out
apps/web/.env*.local

# Scan output — a structured map of a repo's internals should never be committed
# by default (see SECURITY.md / plan §Security "Generated-output hygiene")
.context/
*.context.db

# Local dev SQLite stores (accounts, repo connections, etc.) — created
# wherever a binary happens to be run from if its own *_DB env var isn't
# set; never intended to be committed.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Team/dev-only gotchas, decisions, and knowledge notes — internal engineering
# context, not something to ship in a repo that may end up in a client's hands.
# Kept locally (agentops note still writes here), just not committed.
.agentops/notes/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Secrets — never commit real credentials
.env
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
Caddyfile
/secrets/

# agentops generated scan output
repo-map.md

# Downloaded embedding model cache (multi-GB, fastembed's local cache dir)
.fastembed_cache/

# `agentops-ruler-bridge::build_ruler_dir`'s own generated source dir —
# regenerated fresh by every `agentops install`/`connect` run, byte-for-byte
# derived from AGENTS.md + the embedded prompt pack. Caught live: two of its
# files ended up committed by mistake in an earlier session (harmless
# content, but still generated output, not source).
.ruler/

# Local, per-developer coding-tool config a contributor's own
# `agentops install`/`connect --remote <url>` run creates against *this*
# repo while dogfooding it — never something to ship, and can contain a
# real local network address (caught live: a contributor's own LAN IP was
# sitting untracked here, one `git add -A` away from being committed).
# `.claude/agents`/`.claude/skills`/`.cursor/agents`/`.cursor/skills` above
# are Ruler's own managed block; these four are written outside Ruler
# (`.mcp.json`/`.codex`/`.gemini`) or aren't Ruler-managed at all
# (`settings.local.json`, a Claude Code permissions/approvals file some
# contributors' global gitignore already covers, but the repo shouldn't
# depend on that).
/.mcp.json
/.mcp.json.bak
/.cursor/mcp.json
/.cursor/mcp.json.bak
/.codex/
/.gemini/
.claude/settings.local.json


# START Ruler Generated Files
/.claude/agents
/.claude/skills
/.cursor/agents
/.cursor/skills
/AGENTS.md
/AGENTS.md.bak
/CLAUDE.md
/CLAUDE.md.bak
# END Ruler Generated Files
